{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_epic_79_mental_poker", "label": "EPIC-79: Mental Poker (research/design spike)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/EPIC-79_Mental_Poker.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_epic_79_mental_poker_mental_poker_concept", "label": "Mental Poker (fair card game with no trusted dealer)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/EPIC-79_Mental_Poker.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Separates two conflated concerns: (1) state coordination \u2014 a replicated state machine over a signed hash-linked event log, no authoritative server; and (2) card secrecy \u2014 the genuinely hard cryptography of a shuffled deck nobody can read. Concern (1) maps cleanly onto pkcore's existing deterministic fold(state, event) engine; concern (2) needs an arkworks stack pkcore deliberately avoids, which drives the crate split."}, {"id": "docs_epic_79_mental_poker_barnett_smart_protocol", "label": "Barnett\u2013Smart Deal-and-Reveal Protocol (VTMF)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/EPIC-79_Mental_Poker.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Threshold ElGamal over a prime-order group: (n,n)-split aggregate key, round-robin verifiable re-mask+permute shuffle, per-card reveal tokens (partial decrypts with Chaum-Pedersen proofs) supporting reveal-to-one (hole cards) and reveal-to-all (board). Proofs at every step make it trustless rather than merely distributed."}, {"id": "docs_epic_79_mental_poker_cardcrypto", "label": "CardCrypto Trait Seam", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/EPIC-79_Mental_Poker.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Associated types for MaskedCard and every proof keep the engine and event schema generic over the crypto scheme; the PlaintextCrypto mock (MaskedCard = Card, proofs = ()) faithfully models l-out-of-l padlock accounting so the whole game loop is testable before any curve arithmetic exists."}, {"id": "docs_epic_79_mental_poker_coordinator", "label": "Coordinator Trait Seam (transport + ordering)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/EPIC-79_Mental_Poker.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Append-and-replay over a signed hash-linked log; the only thing that differs across deployment topologies \u2014 each of the six architectures is one Coordinator impl, so topology can change without touching engine or crypto."}, {"id": "docs_epic_79_mental_poker_signed_event_log", "label": "Signed Hash-Linked Event Log", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/EPIC-79_Mental_Poker.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "prev_hash makes each event commit to the entire history (no reorder/drop/splice); seq + author legality uses the turn structure as the ordering oracle, giving ordering without consensus; equivocation is detectable because conflicting events are signed over the same prev_hash and seq. Generalizes pkcore's existing per-hand TableAction event log with a cryptographic envelope."}, {"id": "docs_epic_79_mental_poker_engine_boundary", "label": "Engine Boundary Invariant (crypto never crosses into the fold)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/EPIC-79_Mental_Poker.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "pkcore's engine only ever sees plaintext Cards and TableActions; signatures, chain-linkage, and crypto proofs are verified at the node boundary. Swapping crypto changes the curve, swapping transport changes topology, and neither touches the engine \u2014 this keeps pkcore free of arkworks dependencies."}, {"id": "docs_epic_79_mental_poker_pkmental", "label": "pkmental Sibling Crate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/EPIC-79_Mental_Poker.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Houses the Barnett-Smart card layer plus thin transport, depending on arkworks; pkcore gets only a future mental-log feature gate (Ed25519 + SHA-256 envelope). Mirrors the pkcore -> pkdealer sibling-repo pattern but with the inverted trust model: pkdealer is a trusted-server gRPC dealer, pkmental is trustless/serverless. Productionizes the throwaway pkcore-mp spike in docs/files/mentalpoker/."}, {"id": "docs_epic_79_mental_poker_deployment_topologies", "label": "Six Deployment Topologies (1 in-proc \u2026 6 fully on-chain)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/EPIC-79_Mental_Poker.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recommended build path 1 -> 3 -> 5: prove crypto in-process, get a playable serverless table over a dumb relay (the literal broadcast channel Barnett-Smart assumes; one ordering point kills equivocation), then add state-channel on-chain settlement once stakes matter. #4 (semi-trusted coordinator) and #6 (fully on-chain SNARK shuffle) are branches off that spine."}, {"id": "docs_epic_79_mental_poker_dropout_problem", "label": "Drop-Out Problem ((n,n) threshold stalling)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/EPIC-79_Mental_Poker.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A player about to lose can stall the hand by withholding their partial decryption; needs timeout events and a forfeiture rule threading through the event log. Settlement (trustless money) and collusion (side-channel hand sharing) are separately flagged: the former is out of scope for v1, the latter unsolvable by crypto."}, {"id": "docs_epic_79_mental_poker_verifiable_shuffle", "label": "Verifiable Shuffle (Bayer\u2013Groth argument)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/EPIC-79_Mental_Poker.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Proof vs argument is a real decision-gate subtlety: a ZK proof can never be forged, an argument of knowledge is sound only against a computationally bounded adversary \u2014 the same assumption public-key crypto already rests on, so the modern reference trades it for ~50 ms prove / <1 ms verify on a 52-card shuffle."}, {"id": "docs_epic_79_mental_poker_qr_transport", "label": "QR Code Transport (experimental Coordinator)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/EPIC-79_Mental_Poker.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A QR shown to the whole table is a physical broadcast channel a player cannot equivocate over. Small per-turn deltas fit one QR (~1-1.5 KB scannable); big one-time objects (masked deck ~3.3 KB, shuffle proofs) need fountain-coded animated QR (RaptorQ), as air-gapped Bitcoin wallets do. Explicitly an experimental idea, not a decision gate."}, {"id": "docs_epic_79_mental_poker_card_game_generalization", "label": "Card-Game Generalization (GameRules + zone/visibility algebra)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/EPIC-79_Mental_Poker.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The clean factoring is not a universal Game object but a layer below: an algebra of card operations over zones (shuffle/deal/move/reveal/peek) plus a zone+visibility model, with family mid-layers (tricktaking, betting, collection). Because CardCrypto already speaks hidden/revealed-to-seat/public, pkmental generalizes to a cardgame-mp by parameterizing over the visibility model \u2014 the same move Royale makes over Kaleidoscope at the protocol level. Hard deferred parts: bidding phases, partnerships, per-game scoring, variable deck sizes, aligning the two cardpack versions (gfcore 0.7.0 vs pkcore 0.6.9)."}, {"id": "docs_epic_79_mental_poker_pkdealer", "label": "pkdealer (trusted-server gRPC dealer)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/EPIC-79_Mental_Poker.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_epic_79_mental_poker_gfcore", "label": "gfcore (Go Fish sibling core)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/EPIC-79_Mental_Poker.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_epic_79_mental_poker_tricktaking", "label": "tricktaking prototype crate (bridge/spades/hearts)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/EPIC-79_Mental_Poker.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://github.com/ImperialBower/tricktaking", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_epic_79_mental_poker_arkworks", "label": "arkworks ecosystem (ark-ec, ark-ff)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/EPIC-79_Mental_Poker.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_epic_79_mental_poker_geometry_mental_poker", "label": "geometryxyz/mental-poker (Rust reference implementation)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/EPIC-79_Mental_Poker.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://github.com/geometryxyz/mental-poker", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_epic_79_mental_poker_sra_1979", "label": "Shamir, Rivest & Adleman: Mental Poker (1979)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "docs/EPIC-79_Mental_Poker.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://people.csail.mit.edu/rivest/pubs/SRA81.pdf", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"i